IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- aia-definitions: Article 3 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by
-- Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), "Definitions": one function for each defined term, 70 in all ((1) to (68), (14a), (14b)).
-- READ-ONLY for the parts. They call these functions to decide whether a thing is a provider, a deployer, a high-risk
-- "safety component" and so on, and pass the facts a person could state.
--
-- How to read a result.
-- Every definition here says "means", so each function returns a BOOLEAN. TRUE: the facts meet every element of the
-- definition. FALSE: the facts do not, and that is the text's own "no" (FALSE-kind: "'X' means ..."), never a guess.
-- A function NEVER answers "the Regulation is silent": where a definition borrows a term from another instrument
-- (a "harmonised standard", "personal data", "critical infrastructure") the borrowed fact is an input, named for that
-- instrument, and the function returns what it is told.
-- A definition that uses another defined term takes that term as a BOOLEAN input named for it ("... is a remote biometric
-- identification system"); the caller computes that input with the function of the other definition.
-- Only (14), (14a) and (14b) take `the date asked`: the Omnibus replaced (14) and inserted (14a) and (14b), so the date
-- selects the text (as enacted before 27 July 2026, as amended from then; aia-timeline.l4). Every other definition is
-- the same in both texts and takes no date. A definition is not gated by Article 113: it applies with the provision
-- that uses it (assumed, not ruled; see NOTES.md, forks F-3-gate).
-- Reading marks: "-- FALSE-kind (...)" and "-- NOTHING-kind (...)" follow the rule of 2026-10-29; "-- fork F-3-n" points
-- at the fork register in NOTES.md.

§ `Article 3(1) to (8): the AI system and the roles`

-- src:66 | (1) ‘AI system’ means a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy and that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment, and that, for explicit or implicit objectives, infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions that can influence physical or virtual environments;
@ref Art 3(1) (src:66)
-- The clause "that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment" says what a system MAY do; it is not a condition a system must meet
-- (recital 12 reads the same way: "could exhibit"). fork F-3-1.
GIVEN `the system is machine-based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the system is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for explicit or implicit objectives, the system infers from the input it receives how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations or decisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those outputs can influence physical or virtual environments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(1) the system is an AI system` MEANS
        `the system is machine-based`
    AND `the system is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy`
    AND `for explicit or implicit objectives, the system infers from the input it receives how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations or decisions`
    AND `those outputs can influence physical or virtual environments`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'AI system' means a machine-based system that ..."

-- src:67 | (2) ‘risk’ means the combination of the probability of an occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm;
@ref Art 3(2) (src:67)
-- "Risk" is a combination of two things; the text gives no formula, so the encoding keeps them as the two typed parts.
-- The probability is a NUMBER from 0 to 1; the severity is the degree the person assessing the harm assigns, as a NUMBER on the scale that person uses.
DECLARE `Art 3(2) risk` HAS
    `probability of an occurrence of harm` IS A NUMBER
    `severity of that harm`                IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the probability of an occurrence of harm` IS A NUMBER
      `the severity of that harm` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Art 3(2) risk`
`Art 3(2) the risk is the combination of probability and severity` MEANS
    `Art 3(2) risk` `the probability of an occurrence of harm` `the severity of that harm`

-- src:68 | (3) ‘provider’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body that develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed and places it on the market or puts the AI system into service under its own name or trademark, whether for payment or free of charge;
@ref Art 3(3) (src:68)
-- fork F-3-3: "develops ... or has ... developed and places it on the market or puts ... into service under its own name or trademark".
-- Read as: whoever develops, or has developed, an AI system or general-purpose AI model AND places it on the market or puts
-- the AI system into service under its own name or trademark. The other reading: whoever develops one is a provider without more.
GIVEN `the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party does so under its own name or trademark` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(3) the party is a provider` MEANS
        (`the party develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` OR `the party has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed`)
    AND `the party places it on the market, or puts the AI system into service`
    AND `the party does so under its own name or trademark`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'provider' means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body that ..." ("whether for payment or free of charge" limits nothing)

-- src:69 | (4) ‘deployer’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body using an AI system under its authority except where the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity;
@ref Art 3(4) (src:69)
GIVEN `the party uses an AI system under its authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(4) the party is a deployer` MEANS
        `the party uses an AI system under its authority`
    AND (NOT `the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'deployer' means ... using an AI system under its authority except where the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity"

-- src:70 | (5) ‘authorised representative’ means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union who has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model to, respectively, perform and carry out on its behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation;
@ref Art 3(5) (src:70)
GIVEN `the party is located or established` IS A `Place of a party`
      `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(5) the party is an authorised representative` MEANS
        `the party is located or established` EQUALS `Established or located in the Union`
    AND `the party has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model`
    AND `the mandate is to perform and carry out on the provider's behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'authorised representative' means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union who has received and accepted a written mandate ..."

-- src:71 | (6) ‘importer’ means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union that places on the market an AI system that bears the name or trademark of a natural or legal person established in a third country;
@ref Art 3(6) (src:71)
GIVEN `the party is located or established` IS A `Place of a party`
      `the party places an AI system on the market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system bears the name or trademark of a natural or legal person established in a third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(6) the party is an importer` MEANS
        `the party is located or established` EQUALS `Established or located in the Union`
    AND `the party places an AI system on the market`
    AND `the AI system bears the name or trademark of a natural or legal person established in a third country`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'importer' means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union that places on the market an AI system that bears the name or trademark of a ... person established in a third country"

-- src:72 | (7) ‘distributor’ means a natural or legal person in the supply chain, other than the provider or the importer, that makes an AI system available on the Union market;
@ref Art 3(7) (src:72)
GIVEN `the party is in the supply chain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is the provider of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is the importer of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party makes the AI system available on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(7) the party is a distributor` MEANS
        `the party is in the supply chain`
    AND (NOT `the party is the provider of the AI system`)
    AND (NOT `the party is the importer of the AI system`)
    AND `the party makes the AI system available on the Union market`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'distributor' means a natural or legal person in the supply chain, other than the provider or the importer, that makes an AI system available on the Union market"

-- src:73 | (8) ‘operator’ means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor;
@ref Art 3(8) (src:73)
-- The role Operator stands for any of the six roles of the text, so it is TRUE.
GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(8) the role is an operator` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN Provider THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Product manufacturer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Deployer THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Authorised representative` THEN TRUE
    WHEN Importer THEN TRUE
    WHEN Distributor THEN TRUE
    WHEN Operator THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Notified body` THEN FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'operator' means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor"
    WHEN `Affected person` THEN FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'operator' means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor"

§ `Article 3(9) to (13): placing on the market, making available, putting into service, intended purpose, misuse`

-- src:74 | (9) ‘placing on the market’ means the first making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market;
@ref Art 3(9) (src:74)
GIVEN `the supply is a making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the first making available of that AI system or model on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(9) the supply is a placing on the market` MEANS
        `the supply is a making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market`
    AND `it is the first making available of that AI system or model on the Union market`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'placing on the market' means the first making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market"

-- src:75 | (10) ‘making available on the market’ means the supply of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model for distribution or use on the Union market in the course of a commercial activity, whether in return for payment or free of charge;
@ref Art 3(10) (src:75)
-- "whether in return for payment or free of charge" limits nothing: payment is not an element.
GIVEN `the supply is of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model for distribution or use on the Union market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply is in the course of a commercial activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(10) the supply is a making available on the market` MEANS
        `the supply is of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model for distribution or use on the Union market`
    AND `the supply is in the course of a commercial activity`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'making available on the market' means the supply of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model for distribution or use on the Union market in the course of a commercial activity"

-- src:76 | (11) ‘putting into service’ means the supply of an AI system for first use directly to the deployer or for own use in the Union for its intended purpose;
@ref Art 3(11) (src:76)
GIVEN `the supply is of an AI system for first use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply is directly to the deployer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply is for own use in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first use is for the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(11) the supply is a putting into service` MEANS
        `the supply is of an AI system for first use`
    AND (`the supply is directly to the deployer` OR `the supply is for own use in the Union`)
    AND `the first use is for the intended purpose of the AI system`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'putting into service' means the supply of an AI system for first use directly to the deployer or for own use in the Union for its intended purpose"

-- src:77 | (12) ‘intended purpose’ means the use for which an AI system is intended by the provider, including the specific context and conditions of use, as specified in the information supplied by the provider in the instructions for use, promotional or sales materials and statements, as well as in the technical documentation;
@ref Art 3(12) (src:77)
-- The text names three kinds of source and the technical documentation; the use counts as specified if any of them specifies it. fork F-3-12.
GIVEN `the use is the use for which the provider intends the AI system, including the specific context and conditions of use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is specified in the instructions for use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is specified in promotional or sales materials and statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is specified in the technical documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(12) the use is the intended purpose` MEANS
        `the use is the use for which the provider intends the AI system, including the specific context and conditions of use`
    AND (`it is specified in the instructions for use` OR `it is specified in promotional or sales materials and statements` OR `it is specified in the technical documentation`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'intended purpose' means the use for which an AI system is intended by the provider ... as specified in the information supplied by the provider in ..."

-- src:78 | (13) ‘reasonably foreseeable misuse’ means the use of an AI system in a way that is not in accordance with its intended purpose, but which may result from reasonably foreseeable human behaviour or interaction with other systems, including other AI systems;
@ref Art 3(13) (src:78)
GIVEN `the use is in a way that is not in accordance with the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use may result from reasonably foreseeable human behaviour or interaction with other systems, including other AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(13) the use is a reasonably foreseeable misuse` MEANS
        `the use is in a way that is not in accordance with the intended purpose of the AI system`
    AND `the use may result from reasonably foreseeable human behaviour or interaction with other systems, including other AI systems`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'reasonably foreseeable misuse' means the use of an AI system in a way that is not in accordance with its intended purpose, but which may result from ..."

§ `Article 3(14), (14a), (14b): safety component, SME, small mid-cap enterprise (the Omnibus replaced one and inserted two)`

-- src:80 | (14) ‘safety component’ means a component of a product or of an AI system which fulfils a safety function for that product or AI system, or the failure or malfunctioning of which endangers the health and safety of persons or property; for the purposes of this definition, a component fulfils a safety function where its intended purpose is to prevent or mitigate risks to health and safety of persons or property;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:463 | ‘safety component’ means a component of a product or of an AI system which fulfils a safety function for that product or AI system, or the failure or malfunctioning of which endangers the health and safety of persons or property;
@ref Art 3(14) (src:80) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:463)
-- VERSION as enacted: a component "fulfils a safety function" in whatever sense the term has (the text leaves it open); an
-- input says whether it does. VERSION as amended: the Omnibus says when it does: where its intended purpose is to prevent or
-- mitigate risks to health and safety of persons or property. The two texts differ for a component that someone says
-- fulfils a safety function but whose intended purpose is not to prevent or mitigate risk (as enacted TRUE, as amended FALSE
-- unless its failure endangers health and safety). fork F-3-14.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the component is a component of a product or of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it fulfils a safety function for that product or AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its failure or malfunctioning endangers the health and safety of persons or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its intended purpose is to prevent or mitigate risks to health and safety of persons or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(14) the component is a safety component` MEANS
    IF NOT `the component is a component of a product or of an AI system`
    THEN FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'safety component' means a component of a product or of an AI system which ..."
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                                       -- VERSION as enacted
            (`it fulfils a safety function for that product or AI system` OR `its failure or malfunctioning endangers the health and safety of persons or property`)
        WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                                       -- VERSION as amended
            (`its intended purpose is to prevent or mitigate risks to health and safety of persons or property` OR `its failure or malfunctioning endangers the health and safety of persons or property`)

-- src:82 | (14a) ‘micro, small and medium-sized enterprise’ or ‘SME’ means a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC;
@ref Art 3(14a) (src:82)
-- The Recommendation is another instrument, so whether the enterprise is one "as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to
-- Recommendation 2003/361/EC" is a borrowed fact (an input).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3(14a) the enterprise is a micro, small and medium-sized enterprise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): point (14a) is not in the text as enacted
    WHEN `as amended` THEN JUST `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC`  -- VERSION as amended. FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'micro, small and medium-sized enterprise' or 'SME' means ..."

-- src:83 | (14b) ‘small mid-cap enterprise’ or ‘SMC’ means a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099;
@ref Art 3(14b) (src:83)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3(14b) the enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
    WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): point (14b) is not in the text as enacted
    WHEN `as amended` THEN JUST `the enterprise is a small mid-cap enterprise as defined in point (2) of the Annex to Recommendation (EU) 2025/1099`  -- VERSION as amended. FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'small mid-cap enterprise' or 'SMC' means ..."

§ `Article 3(15) to (28): instructions, recall, withdrawal, performance, authorities, conformity, modification, marking, monitoring, standards`

-- src:85 | (15) ‘instructions for use’ means the information provided by the provider to inform the deployer of, in particular, an AI system’s intended purpose and proper use;
@ref Art 3(15) (src:85)
GIVEN `the information is provided by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provided to inform the deployer of the intended purpose and proper use of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(15) the information is instructions for use` MEANS
        `the information is provided by the provider`
    AND `it is provided to inform the deployer of the intended purpose and proper use of the AI system`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'instructions for use' means the information provided by the provider to inform the deployer of, in particular, ..." ("in particular" adds examples, not elements)

-- src:86 | (16) ‘recall of an AI system’ means any measure aiming to achieve the return to the provider or taking out of service or disabling the use of an AI system made available to deployers;
@ref Art 3(16) (src:86)
GIVEN `the measure aims to achieve the return of an AI system to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure aims to take an AI system out of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure aims to disable the use of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system was made available to deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(16) the measure is a recall of an AI system` MEANS
        (`the measure aims to achieve the return of an AI system to the provider` OR `the measure aims to take an AI system out of service` OR `the measure aims to disable the use of an AI system`)
    AND `the AI system was made available to deployers`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'recall of an AI system' means any measure aiming to achieve the return to the provider or taking out of service or disabling the use of an AI system made available to deployers"

-- src:87 | (17) ‘withdrawal of an AI system’ means any measure aiming to prevent an AI system in the supply chain being made available on the market;
@ref Art 3(17) (src:87)
GIVEN `the measure aims to prevent an AI system in the supply chain being made available on the market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(17) the measure is a withdrawal of an AI system` MEANS
    `the measure aims to prevent an AI system in the supply chain being made available on the market`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'withdrawal of an AI system' means any measure aiming to prevent an AI system in the supply chain being made available on the market"

-- src:88 | (18) ‘performance of an AI system’ means the ability of an AI system to achieve its intended purpose;
@ref Art 3(18) (src:88)
GIVEN `the quality is the ability of an AI system to achieve its intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(18) the quality is the performance of an AI system` MEANS
    `the quality is the ability of an AI system to achieve its intended purpose`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'performance of an AI system' means the ability of an AI system to achieve its intended purpose"

-- src:89 | (19) ‘notifying authority’ means the national authority responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring;
@ref Art 3(19) (src:89)
GIVEN `the authority is a national authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(19) the authority is a notifying authority` MEANS
        `the authority is a national authority`
    AND `it is responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'notifying authority' means the national authority responsible for ..."

-- src:90 | (20) ‘conformity assessment’ means the process of demonstrating whether the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 relating to a high-risk AI system have been fulfilled;
@ref Art 3(20) (src:90)
GIVEN `the process is a process of demonstrating whether requirements have been fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements are those set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they relate to a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(20) the process is a conformity assessment` MEANS
        `the process is a process of demonstrating whether requirements have been fulfilled`
    AND `the requirements are those set out in Chapter III, Section 2`
    AND `they relate to a high-risk AI system`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'conformity assessment' means the process of demonstrating whether the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 relating to a high-risk AI system have been fulfilled"

-- src:91 | (21) ‘conformity assessment body’ means a body that performs third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection;
@ref Art 3(21) (src:91)
-- "including testing, certification and inspection" gives examples; the element is third-party conformity assessment activities.
GIVEN `the body performs third-party conformity assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(21) the body is a conformity assessment body` MEANS
    `the body performs third-party conformity assessment activities`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'conformity assessment body' means a body that performs third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection"

-- src:92 | (22) ‘notified body’ means a conformity assessment body notified in accordance with this Regulation and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation;
@ref Art 3(22) (src:92)
-- fork F-3-22: "in accordance with this Regulation and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation" is read as both,
-- where the other legislation provides for notification at all; where none is relevant the input is TRUE.
GIVEN `the body is a conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(22) the body is a notified body` MEANS
        `the body is a conformity assessment body`
    AND `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation`
    AND `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'notified body' means a conformity assessment body notified in accordance with this Regulation and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation"

-- src:93 | (23) ‘substantial modification’ means a change to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service which is not foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider and as a result of which the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected or results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed;
@ref Art 3(23) (src:93)
GIVEN `the change is to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(23) the change is a substantial modification` MEANS
        `the change is to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service`
    AND (NOT `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider`)
    AND (`as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` OR `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'substantial modification' means a change to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service which is not foreseen or planned ..."

-- src:94 | (24) ‘CE marking’ means a marking by which a provider indicates that an AI system is in conformity with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 and other applicable Union harmonisation legislation providing for its affixing;
@ref Art 3(24) (src:94)
GIVEN `the marking is a marking by which a provider indicates something` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indicates that an AI system is in conformity with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indicates conformity with other applicable Union harmonisation legislation providing for its affixing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
