§ `Article 3(53) to (60): plans, sandboxes, literacy, real-world testing, consent, deep fakes`

-- src:129 | (53) ‘real-world testing plan’ means a document that describes the objectives, methodology, geographical, population and temporal scope, monitoring, organisation and conduct of testing in real-world conditions;
@ref Art 3(53) (src:129)
-- All eight things must be described. The document describes them "of testing in real-world conditions".
DECLARE `Art 3(53) what a real-world testing plan describes` HAS
    `objectives`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `methodology`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `geographical scope`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `population scope`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `temporal scope`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `monitoring`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `organisation`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `conduct`                  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Art 3(53) (src:129)
GIVEN `the thing is a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions` IS A `Art 3(53) what a real-world testing plan describes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(53) the document is a real-world testing plan` MEANS
        `the thing is a document`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `objectives`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `methodology`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `geographical scope`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `population scope`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `temporal scope`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `monitoring`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `organisation`
    AND `what the document describes of testing in real-world conditions`'s `conduct`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'real-world testing plan' means a document that describes the objectives, methodology, geographical, population and temporal scope, monitoring, organisation and conduct of testing in real-world conditions"

-- src:130 | (54) ‘sandbox plan’ means a document agreed between the participating provider and the competent authority describing the objectives, conditions, timeframe, methodology and requirements for the activities carried out within the sandbox;
@ref Art 3(54) (src:130)
DECLARE `Art 3(54) what a sandbox plan describes` HAS
    `objectives`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `conditions`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `timeframe`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `methodology`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `requirements` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Art 3(54) (src:130)
GIVEN `the thing is a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is agreed between the participating provider and the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the document describes for the activities carried out within the sandbox` IS A `Art 3(54) what a sandbox plan describes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(54) the document is a sandbox plan` MEANS
        `the thing is a document`
    AND `it is agreed between the participating provider and the competent authority`
    AND `what the document describes for the activities carried out within the sandbox`'s `objectives`
    AND `what the document describes for the activities carried out within the sandbox`'s `conditions`
    AND `what the document describes for the activities carried out within the sandbox`'s `timeframe`
    AND `what the document describes for the activities carried out within the sandbox`'s `methodology`
    AND `what the document describes for the activities carried out within the sandbox`'s `requirements`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'sandbox plan' means a document agreed between the participating provider and the competent authority describing the objectives, conditions, timeframe, methodology and requirements for the activities carried out within the sandbox"

-- src:131 | (55) ‘AI regulatory sandbox’ means a controlled framework set up by a competent authority which offers providers or prospective providers of AI systems the possibility to develop, train, validate and test, where appropriate in real-world conditions, an innovative AI system, pursuant to a sandbox plan for a limited time under regulatory supervision;
@ref Art 3(55) (src:131)
GIVEN `the framework is a controlled framework` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is set up by a competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it offers providers or prospective providers of AI systems the possibility to develop, train, validate and test an innovative AI system, where appropriate in real-world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so pursuant to a sandbox plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so for a limited time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so under regulatory supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(55) the framework is an AI regulatory sandbox` MEANS
        `the framework is a controlled framework`
    AND `it is set up by a competent authority`
    AND `it offers providers or prospective providers of AI systems the possibility to develop, train, validate and test an innovative AI system, where appropriate in real-world conditions`
    AND `it does so pursuant to a sandbox plan`
    AND `it does so for a limited time`
    AND `it does so under regulatory supervision`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'AI regulatory sandbox' means a controlled framework set up by a competent authority which offers providers or prospective providers of AI systems the possibility to develop, train, validate and test ..."

-- src:132 | (56) ‘AI literacy’ means skills, knowledge and understanding that allow providers, deployers and affected persons, taking into account their respective rights and obligations in the context of this Regulation, to make an informed deployment of AI systems, as well as to gain awareness about the opportunities and risks of AI and possible harm it can cause;
@ref Art 3(56) (src:132)
GIVEN `the things are skills, knowledge and understanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they allow providers, deployers and affected persons, taking into account their respective rights and obligations in the context of this Regulation, to make an informed deployment of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they allow them to gain awareness about the opportunities and risks of AI and possible harm it can cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(56) the things are AI literacy` MEANS
        `the things are skills, knowledge and understanding`
    AND `they allow providers, deployers and affected persons, taking into account their respective rights and obligations in the context of this Regulation, to make an informed deployment of AI systems`
    AND `they allow them to gain awareness about the opportunities and risks of AI and possible harm it can cause`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'AI literacy' means skills, knowledge and understanding that allow providers, deployers and affected persons ... to make an informed deployment of AI systems, as well as to gain awareness ..."

-- src:133 | (57) ‘testing in real-world conditions’ means the temporary testing of an AI system for its intended purpose in real-world conditions outside a laboratory or otherwise simulated environment, with a view to gathering reliable and robust data and to assessing and verifying the conformity of the AI system with the requirements of this Regulation and it does not qualify as placing the AI system on the market or putting it into service within the meaning of this Regulation, provided that all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled;
@ref Art 3(57) (src:133)
-- The conditions of Article 57 or 60 are another part's rules (P5, P6): their outcome is an input.
GIVEN `the testing is temporary testing of an AI system for its intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in real-world conditions outside a laboratory or otherwise simulated environment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is with a view to gathering reliable and robust data and to assessing and verifying the conformity of the AI system with the requirements of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(57) the testing is testing in real-world conditions` MEANS
        `the testing is temporary testing of an AI system for its intended purpose`
    AND `it is in real-world conditions outside a laboratory or otherwise simulated environment`
    AND `it is with a view to gathering reliable and robust data and to assessing and verifying the conformity of the AI system with the requirements of this Regulation`
    AND `all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'testing in real-world conditions' means the temporary testing of an AI system for its intended purpose in real-world conditions outside a laboratory ... provided that all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled"

-- "and it does not qualify as placing the AI system on the market or putting it into service ... provided that all the conditions ... are fulfilled".
-- A grant limited by its own wording: where the conditions are not all fulfilled the text says nothing about whether the testing is a placing on the market.
@ref Art 3(57) (src:133)
GIVEN `the testing is testing in real-world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 3(57) the testing does not qualify as placing on the market or putting into service` MEANS
    IF `the testing is testing in real-world conditions` AND `all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided that all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled"; the text does not say the testing then qualifies as a placing on the market

-- src:134 | (58) ‘subject’, for the purpose of real-world testing, means a natural person who participates in testing in real-world conditions;
@ref Art 3(58) (src:134)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person participates in testing in real-world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(58) the person is a subject for the purpose of real-world testing` MEANS
        `the person is a natural person`
    AND `the person participates in testing in real-world conditions`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'subject', for the purpose of real-world testing, means a natural person who participates in testing in real-world conditions"

-- src:135 | (59) ‘informed consent’ means a subject’s freely given, specific, unambiguous and voluntary expression of his or her willingness to participate in a particular testing in real-world conditions, after having been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to the subject’s decision to participate;
@ref Art 3(59) (src:135)
DECLARE `Art 3(59) how a subject expressed willingness` HAS
    `freely given`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `specific`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `unambiguous`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntary`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `to participate in a particular testing in real-world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `after being informed of all aspects of the testing relevant to the decision to participate` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Art 3(59) (src:135)
GIVEN `the person is a subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expression is by the subject of willingness` IS A `Art 3(59) how a subject expressed willingness`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(59) the expression is an informed consent` MEANS
        `the person is a subject`
    AND `the expression is by the subject of willingness`'s `freely given`
    AND `the expression is by the subject of willingness`'s `specific`
    AND `the expression is by the subject of willingness`'s `unambiguous`
    AND `the expression is by the subject of willingness`'s `voluntary`
    AND `the expression is by the subject of willingness`'s `to participate in a particular testing in real-world conditions`
    AND `the expression is by the subject of willingness`'s `after being informed of all aspects of the testing relevant to the decision to participate`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'informed consent' means a subject's freely given, specific, unambiguous and voluntary expression of his or her willingness to participate in a particular testing in real-world conditions, after having been informed of all aspects ..."

-- src:136 | (60) ‘deep fake’ means AI-generated or manipulated image, audio or video content that resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events and would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful;
@ref Art 3(60) (src:136)
GIVEN `the content is AI-generated or manipulated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is image, audio or video content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(60) the content is a deep fake` MEANS
        `the content is AI-generated or manipulated`
    AND `it is image, audio or video content`
    AND `it resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events`
    AND `it would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'deep fake' means AI-generated or manipulated image, audio or video content that resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events and would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful"

§ `Article 3(61) and (62): widespread infringement and critical infrastructure`

-- src:137 | (61) ‘widespread infringement’ means any act or omission contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals, which:
-- src:138 | (a) has harmed or is likely to harm the collective interests of individuals residing in at least two Member States other than the Member State in which:
-- src:139 | (i) the act or omission originated or took place;
-- src:140 | (ii) the provider concerned, or, where applicable, its authorised representative is located or established; or
-- src:141 | (iii) the deployer is established, when the infringement is committed by the deployer;
-- src:142 | (b) has caused, causes or is likely to cause harm to the collective interests of individuals and has common features, including the same unlawful practice or the same interest being infringed, and is occurring concurrently, committed by the same operator, in at least three Member States;
@ref Art 3(61) (src:137-142)
-- fork F-3-61: limbs (a) and (b) end with semicolons and no "or"/"and", so the text does not say whether they are alternatives.
-- Read as alternatives (assumed, not ruled); the other reading is that both must hold.
-- Limb (a) counts the Member States other than the three named in (a)(i) to (iii): the caller subtracts those.
GIVEN `the act or omission is contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Member States, other than those named in (a)(i) to (iii), in which individuals residing there have been harmed or are likely to be harmed in their collective interests` IS A NUMBER
      `the harm to the collective interests of individuals has been caused, is caused or is likely to be caused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the infringement has common features, including the same unlawful practice or the same interest being infringed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is occurring concurrently, committed by the same operator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Member States in which it is occurring` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(61) the act or omission is a widespread infringement` MEANS
        `the act or omission is contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals`
    AND (   `the number of Member States, other than those named in (a)(i) to (iii), in which individuals residing there have been harmed or are likely to be harmed in their collective interests` AT LEAST 2
         OR (    `the harm to the collective interests of individuals has been caused, is caused or is likely to be caused`
             AND `the infringement has common features, including the same unlawful practice or the same interest being infringed`
             AND `it is occurring concurrently, committed by the same operator`
             AND `the number of Member States in which it is occurring` AT LEAST 3))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'widespread infringement' means any act or omission contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals, which: (a) ...; (b) ..."

-- src:143 | (62) ‘critical infrastructure’ means critical infrastructure as defined in Article 2, point (4), of Directive (EU) 2022/2557;
@ref Art 3(62) (src:143)
GIVEN `the infrastructure is critical infrastructure as defined in Article 2, point (4), of Directive (EU) 2022/2557` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(62) the infrastructure is critical infrastructure` MEANS
    `the infrastructure is critical infrastructure as defined in Article 2, point (4), of Directive (EU) 2022/2557`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'critical infrastructure' means critical infrastructure as defined in Article 2, point (4), of Directive (EU) 2022/2557" (borrowed fact)

§ `Article 3(63) to (68): general-purpose AI`

-- src:144 | (63) ‘general-purpose AI model’ means an AI model, including where such an AI model is trained with a large amount of data using self-supervision at scale, that displays significant generality and is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks regardless of the way the model is placed on the market and that can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications, except AI models that are used for research, development or prototyping activities before they are placed on the market;
@ref Art 3(63) (src:144)
-- "including where such an AI model is trained with a large amount of data using self-supervision at scale" says the training
-- method does not matter; it is not an element. "regardless of the way the model is placed on the market" likewise.
GIVEN `the model is an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it displays significant generality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(63) the model is a general-purpose AI model` MEANS
        `the model is an AI model`
    AND `it displays significant generality`
    AND `it is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks`
    AND `it can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications`
    AND (NOT `it is used for research, development or prototyping activities before it is placed on the market`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'general-purpose AI model' means an AI model ... that displays significant generality ... except AI models that are used for research, development or prototyping activities before they are placed on the market"

-- src:145 | (64) ‘high-impact capabilities’ means capabilities that match or exceed the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models;
@ref Art 3(64) (src:145)
GIVEN `the capabilities match the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capabilities exceed the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(64) the capabilities are high-impact capabilities` MEANS
    `the capabilities match the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models` OR `the capabilities exceed the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'high-impact capabilities' means capabilities that match or exceed the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models"

-- src:146 | (65) ‘systemic risk’ means a risk that is specific to the high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models, having a significant impact on the Union market due to their reach, or due to actual or reasonably foreseeable negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights, or the society as a whole, that can be propagated at scale across the value chain;
@ref Art 3(65) (src:146)
GIVEN `the thing is a risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is specific to the high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a significant impact on the Union market due to the reach of those models` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a significant impact due to actual or reasonably foreseeable negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights, or the society as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be propagated at scale across the value chain` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(65) the risk is a systemic risk` MEANS
        `the thing is a risk`
    AND `it is specific to the high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models`
    AND (`it has a significant impact on the Union market due to the reach of those models` OR `it has a significant impact due to actual or reasonably foreseeable negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights, or the society as a whole`)
    AND `it can be propagated at scale across the value chain`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'systemic risk' means a risk that is specific to the high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models, having a significant impact on the Union market due to their reach, or due to actual or reasonably foreseeable negative effects ... that can be propagated at scale across the value chain"

-- src:147 | (66) ‘general-purpose AI system’ means an AI system which is based on a general-purpose AI model and which has the capability to serve a variety of purposes, both for direct use as well as for integration in other AI systems;
@ref Art 3(66) (src:147)
GIVEN `the AI system is an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is based on a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has the capability to serve a variety of purposes, both for direct use and for integration in other AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(66) the AI system is a general-purpose AI system` MEANS
        `the AI system is an AI system`
    AND `it is based on a general-purpose AI model`
    AND `it has the capability to serve a variety of purposes, both for direct use and for integration in other AI systems`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'general-purpose AI system' means an AI system which is based on a general-purpose AI model and which has the capability to serve a variety of purposes, both for direct use as well as for integration in other AI systems"

-- src:148 | (67) ‘floating-point operation’ means any mathematical operation or assignment involving floating-point numbers, which are a subset of the real numbers typically represented on computers by an integer of fixed precision scaled by an integer exponent of a fixed base;
@ref Art 3(67) (src:148)
GIVEN `the operation is a mathematical operation or assignment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves floating-point numbers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(67) the operation is a floating-point operation` MEANS
        `the operation is a mathematical operation or assignment`
    AND `it involves floating-point numbers`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'floating-point operation' means any mathematical operation or assignment involving floating-point numbers"

-- src:149 | (68) ‘downstream provider’ means a provider of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system, which integrates an AI model, regardless of whether the AI model is provided by themselves and vertically integrated or provided by another entity based on contractual relations.
@ref Art 3(68) (src:149)
-- "regardless of whether the AI model is provided by themselves and vertically integrated or by another entity" says the model's source does not matter.
GIVEN `the party is a provider of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system integrates an AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 3(68) the party is a downstream provider` MEANS
        `the party is a provider of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system`
    AND `the AI system integrates an AI model`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'downstream provider' means a provider of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system, which integrates an AI model, regardless of ..."
